Appendix E: Deployment Door Structural Penalty Analysis

E.1 Door Mass Estimation Models

E.1.1 Slot Door (Pez Dispenser):

The structural penalty of a narrow slot is concentrated in the local reinforcement around the opening. Using simple pressure vessel theory for a cylinder with a rectangular cutout:

\Delta M_{\text{slot}} \approx \rho_{\text{structure}} \cdot A_{\text{reinforcement}} \cdot t_{\text{reinforcement}}

where A_{\text{reinforcement}} is the area of reinforcement around the slot, and t_{\text{reinforcement}} is the additional thickness required to maintain structural integrity.

For a slot of width w and height h in a cylinder of radius R:

A_{\text{reinforcement}} \approx 2(w + h) \cdot L_{\text{transition}}

where L_{\text{transition}} \approx 2\sqrt{R t} is the characteristic length over which stresses redistribute (the "decay length" in shell theory).

E.1.2 Clamshell Door (Chomper):

The chomper door introduces a large opening that significantly weakens the cylindrical shell. The mass penalty includes:

1. Door mass: \Delta M_{\text{door}} = \rho_{\text{structure}} \cdot A_{\text{door}} \cdot t_{\text{door}}
2. Hinge and latching mechanism mass
3. Stiffening rings around the opening
4. Thermal sealing system

For a door spanning the full diameter (D = 8 m) and extending L_{\text{door}} = 14 m:

A_{\text{door}} \approx D \cdot L_{\text{door}} = 8 \times 14 = 112 \text{ m}^2

With t_{\text{door}} = 5 mm aluminum (assumed for stiffness):

M_{\text{door}} = 2,700 \text{ kg/m}^3 \times 112 \text{ m}^2 \times 0.005 \text{ m} = 1,512 \text{ kg}

Adding hinges, latches, and stiffeners: M_{\text{door,total}} \approx 2,000\text{–}3,000 kg.

E.1.3 Hybrid (Slot + Reduced Door):

The hybrid approach combines a slot for small modules with a smaller door for core modules. The mass penalty is:

\Delta M_{\text{hybrid}} = \Delta M_{\text{slot}} + \Delta M_{\text{door,reduced}} + \Delta M_{\text{complexity}}

where \Delta M_{\text{door,reduced}} is for a door sized to the core modules (e.g., 4 m × 6 m rather than full 8 m × 14 m), and \Delta M_{\text{complexity}} accounts for the interaction between the two mechanisms.

E.2 Structural Penalty Comparison

Deployment Option Estimated Mass Penalty % of Dry Mass (assuming 100 t dry) Deployment Capability
Slot only 500–1,000 kg 0.5–1% Small modules only (<1 m)
Door only 2,000–3,000 kg 2–3% All module sizes (up to 8 m)
Hybrid 1,500–2,500 kg 1.5–2.5% Mixed sizes

Note: These are estimates to be refined through detailed FEA in the thesis work. The 15% figure sometimes cited in the literature refers to the Space Shuttle payload bay door system relative to the Orbiter's dry mass, which is not directly applicable to Starship.

