Appendix I: Sensitivity Analysis Framework

I.1 Parameter Sensitivity

For a parameter \theta (e.g., \eta_{\text{packing}}, M_{\text{payload,max}}, t_{\text{shield}}), the sensitivity of the optimal modularity N^* is:

S_{\theta} = \frac{\partial N^* / N^*}{\partial \theta / \theta}

This is estimated numerically by perturbing \theta and re-optimizing.

I.2 Dominant Parameter Identification

The variance-based sensitivity index (Sobol index) for parameter \theta is:

S_\theta = \frac{\text{Var}_{\theta}(E[N^* | \theta])}{\text{Var}(N^*)}

Parameters with high Sobol indices are the dominant drivers of the optimal architecture. Preliminary expectations:

· M_{\text{payload,max}} (Block version): High sensitivity — drives mass constraint
· m_{I} (interface mass): High sensitivity — drives marginal cost of modularity
· t_{\text{shield}} (shielding thickness): Moderate sensitivity — drives habitat module size
· \eta_{\text{packing}}: Moderate sensitivity — drives volume constraint
· \alpha (integration complexity exponent): High sensitivity — drives optimal N

